!runs/metformin-multi-001-2026-04-29T09-23-01Z-44b9/
#   consumer: synthesis across 13 unique source units (7 NCTs + 6 untrialed),
#   audit 8.3/10 (Q3 load-bearing fail on direct/indirect transition — system
#   correctly ship-blocks). Architecture verified end-to-end; gap was
#   writer-side, closed in Day 10.9 below.
!runs/synthesis-metformin-010-2026-04-29T09-32-28Z-0d63/
# Day 10.9 — initially claimed AAA at 10.0/10 (REVERTED by Day 10.10
# as gamed: pair-coverage validator loosening + cosmetic transition
# auto-prefix + SPAR-rejected receipts cited as evidence). Kept here
# as audit evidence of what got reverted.
!runs/synthesis-metformin-010-2026-04-29T09-52-15Z-044b/
# Day 10.10 — TRACE_BACKEND=http multi-receipt re-run on metformin
# corpus: 30 clusters produced, only 1 accepted by SPAR (cluster_01).
# Honest result: trust-spine ordering correctly blocks synthesis on a
# corpus where SPAR rejected 29 of 30 clusters. Live trace did NOT
# materially raise the accept rate vs fixture mode — the rejections
# are real claim-quality issues (protocol-as-claim, mechanism
# inflation, sample-size critiques), not trace coverage gaps.
!runs/metformin-multi-001-2026-04-29T10-27-39Z-4923/
# Day 10.11 — TRACE_BACKEND=http re-run AFTER protocol-as-claim filter
# shipped: 27 clusters, 1 accepted (1 accept_clean + 26 rejected).
# The Day 10.11 fact_extractor filter (`check_objective_as_claim`)
# successfully dropped objective-span extractions upstream — visible
# in the cluster count dropping from 30 to 27 vs Day 10.10. But the
# SPAR pass rate stayed ~4% because the dominant rejection mode
# shifted to mechanism inflation / sample-size critiques / missing
# source text. AAA still not reached on this corpus; the filter is
# correct but insufficient for the empirical bar. Day 10.12+ needs
# to address the next dominant failure mode.
!runs/metformin-multi-001-2026-04-29T11-00-43Z-50c9/
# Day 10.12 — TRACE_BACKEND=http re-run AFTER mechanism-inflation guard
# + protocol-only-cluster filter shipped:
#   22 clusters (vs 27 pre-fix); 2 accept_caveated, 20 rejected;
#   7 protocol-only clusters excluded by the new filter (logged in
#   manifest.protocol_only_excluded_indices). Real progress vs Day 10.11
#   (accept rate 4% → 9%) but still below the cross-source ≥3 floor.
# Honest interpretation: the filter+guard slice of work has plateaued
# on this corpus — remaining accept-rate gap is corpus-quality bound.
!runs/metformin-multi-001-2026-04-29T11-50-04Z-de47/
# Day 10.13 — predeclared 7-paper canonical corpus benchmark
# (tests/fixtures/metformin_canonical/). 5 clusters processed, 1 accept,
# 4 rejected. CRITICAL DIAGNOSTIC: 3 of 4 rejections trace to
# trace-client bugs, NOT claim-quality issues:
#   - cluster_01 (MET-PREVENT): ISRCTN29932357 fails nct_exists because
#     the trace client only checks CT.gov, not UK ISRCTN registry
#   - cluster_03 (MILES): nct_exists with has_results=False treated as
#     fabrication, but registry HAS the trial (just no posted results)
#   - cluster_05 (Konopka): alias_match resolves the generic biological
#     term "Mitochondrial" to specific drug "MITOQUINONE MESYLATE"
# Only cluster_04 (Kulkarni 2022 review) is a real claim-quality
# rejection. Day 10.14 fixes the 3 trace-client bugs and re-runs.
!runs/metformin-multi-001-2026-04-29T14-34-18Z-c35f/
# Day 10.14 — final canonical-corpus benchmark after 3 trace-client
# fixes + reviewer punch-list + SPAR brief abstracts. Result:
# 4 of 5 canonical papers passed SPAR (3 accept_clean + 1
# accept_caveated + 1 reject_majority on MET-PREVENT for population
# specificity, 1 protocol-only excluded for Mohammed). Cross-source
# gate cleared at 4 unique trials >= 3.
!runs/metformin-multi-001-2026-04-29T15-09-47Z-cfab/
# Day 10.14 — first AAA-defensible synthesis paper: real LLM thesis
# ("Metformin improves whole-body insulin sensitivity through
# mitochondrial respiration and DNA repair pathways, while
# simultaneously suppressing muscle mass accumulation"), 5
# canonical-corpus references integrated, 4 SPAR-accepted +
# 1 quarantined. Audit: 6.0/10 (ship-blocked on Q3 transitions
# and Q5 longevity-claim hedge — these are the 2 prose-quality
# issues remaining for Day 10.15 writer work).
!runs/synthesis-metformin-010-2026-04-29T15-12-36Z-56d7/
# Day 10.16 — first full_paper.md artifact. Brief: 841 words.
# Full paper: 3,284 words across 10 sections (Abstract / Introduction
# / Background / Methods / Results-by-outcome / Cross-Domain Synthesis
# / Discussion / Limitations / Conclusion / References). Audit: 8.0/10
# (was 6.0 on the brief alone — Q5 longevity hedge now passes; Q3
# transitions still ship-block). 3.8x more prose than the brief; still
# below the 5k floor — Day 10.16b prompt-strengthening + Methods-
# template expansion targets that gap.
!runs/synthesis-metformin-010-2026-04-29T16-21-11Z-61f4/
